{"availability":"available","full":"raphaelmansuy/edgeparse","name":"edgeparse","description":"EdgeParse converts any digital PDF into Markdown, JSON (with bounding boxes), HTML, or plain text — deterministically, without a JVM, without a GPU, and with best-in-class accuracy on the 200-document benchmark suite included in this repository.","category":"Productivity","language":"Rust","stars":147,"forks":18,"created":"2026-03-22T08:02:45Z","updated":"2026-10-09T14:19:01Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://edgeparse.com","topics":["markdown","markitdown","pdf","pdf-converter"],"demo":"https://www.edgeparse.com/demo/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:35.067Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:35.067Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:35.067Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T19:51:35.067Z","stars":147,"forks":18}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Fastest PDF extraction engine. Rust-native. No ML stack required for born-digital PDFs; optional in-browser OCR for image tables.","Extract Markdown, JSON (with bounding boxes), and HTML from any born-digital PDF — deterministically, in milliseconds, on CPU.","Never claim a win for engines not finished (Marker, MinerU, Nutrient, Unstructured partial). Benchmark details"],"features":["How accurate is it? — Two labeled boards (2026-10-01, Apple M4 Max, 200 docs):","Official odl-bench (mean(NID,TEDS,MHS)): EdgeParse hybrid 0.900 (leads every finished metric), deterministic 0.857, WASM 0.854.","EdgeParse harness: deterministic 0.782 overall at 0.019 s/doc.","How fast? — 0.02 s/doc deterministic on Apple M4 Max for the 200-document corpus. Hybrid mode is slower (0.81 s/doc) when pages route to a local Docling Fast backend.","Does it need a GPU or Java? — No. No JVM, no GPU, no Python runtime for the CLI. Born-digital PDFs need no OCR models; optional PP-OCRv6 runs in-browser or on Node for image tables. Single 15 MB binary."],"sourceUrl"